N={
"eads25_interspeech":("A child learning to change articulation needs feedback that connects what they feel and see with how their speech sounds.","Articulation is hidden, children vary in development, and feedback must align audio, visual movement, and a usable teaching target without overwhelming the learner.","Show a waveform or give a generic pronunciation score and assume it identifies the movement to change.","Build a multimodal American English child-speech corpus specialized for articulatory feedback, with synchronized speech and articulatory information.","PERCEPT-US provides a multimodal child speech corpus designed for articulatory feedback.","The corpus makes a hidden motor target observable: acoustic output can be related to articulator configuration and learner-facing feedback rather than treated as an isolated sound label.","The paper reports corpus resources and articulatory-feedback-oriented evaluation for American English child speech.","Speakers, ages, tasks, sensor alignment, labels, and corpus size limit generalization; a resource does not itself establish learning or clinical benefit."),
"gorthi25_interspeech":("Biometric anti-spoofing must reject attacks across modalities and conditions while staying light enough for real security systems.","Attack traces differ by sensor and generator, and a heavy multimodal model can be accurate but too slow or too specialized to deploy.","Train a modality-specific detector or use a large model and evaluate only on the attack types seen during training.","Combine lightweight modality-aware representations with generalized anti-spoofing features and test cross-condition biometric security.","LitMAS is a lightweight generalized multimodal anti-spoofing framework for biometric security.","Security is a coverage problem: the model must learn signs of manipulation that survive changes in modality and attack source, while the resource budget constrains the detector itself.","The paper reports generalized multimodal anti-spoofing performance with a lightweight framework.","Biometric modalities, attacks, datasets, fusion, thresholds, and compute budget bound the result; benchmark generalization is not security certification."),
"grigoryan25_interspeech":("An ASR decoder must choose a likely word sequence efficiently, but beam search can miss a better path or spend too much computation on unhelpful alternatives.","Transducer scores are local while the best sequence is global; beam width, pruning, and length effects interact with streaming constraints.","Increase the beam indefinitely or use greedy decoding and assume the accuracy/latency tradeoff is universal.","Analyze and improve beam-search decoding for transducer ASR, testing how search choices affect accuracy and computation.","The paper pushes the limits of beam-search decoding for transducer-based ASR models.","Decoding is an inference budget: the beam is a controlled approximation to sequence search, and improvements come from spending computation where competing hypotheses remain plausible.","The paper reports decoding accuracy and efficiency findings for transducer ASR across the tested search settings.","Model, language, beam policy, pruning, hardware, and streaming setup bound the result; a better beam does not remove acoustic or language-model errors."),
"hartuv25_interspeech":("A speech tokenizer should turn sound into compact units that preserve the information a downstream speech model actually needs.","Acoustic detail, phonetic identity, speaker identity, and temporal precision compete for a limited token budget; reconstruction quality alone may reward irrelevant detail.","Use waveform compression or text-like units and assume the best reconstruction tokenizer is the best speech representation.","Build a phonetic-acoustic tokenizer and evaluate whether its tokens capture both speech sound structure and useful phonetic distinctions.","PAST is a phonetic-acoustic speech tokenizer.","Tokenization is a choice about what survives discretization: units should preserve acoustically grounded, phonetic information while discarding redundant waveform variation.","The paper reports tokenizer quality and downstream speech-representation results for the proposed phonetic-acoustic units.","Token rate, codebook, languages, speakers, reconstruction target, and downstream tasks bound the claim; discrete units are not automatically linguistically complete."),
"hegde25_interspeech":("A dialogue-state tracker should use examples in context effectively, but its ability to learn from a few demonstrations may depend on how the dialogue and prompts are arranged.","State labels, turn order, domain vocabulary, and example selection can change what the model appears to infer from context.","Measure one prompt format and attribute the result to general in-context learning ability.","Systematically vary dialogue-state-tracking factors such as demonstrations, domain, and context to identify which conditions support or break in-context learning.","The paper studies factors affecting the in-context learning abilities of LLMs for dialogue state tracking.","In-context learning is an interaction between model prior and task presentation: the examples are part of the effective program and must be analyzed as such.","The paper reports factor-level findings on in-context dialogue-state tracking.","Model family, prompt, domains, state schema, demonstration order, and context length bound the result; prompt sensitivity is not a stable conversational capability."),
"kumar25c_interspeech":("Speech translation can use articulator movement as an intermediate signal, especially when the sound alone is ambiguous or the target language lacks data.","Articulator space is not directly observed in ordinary speech, and translation must preserve meaning while passing through a representation with its own measurement errors.","Translate acoustic features directly or force a text transcript and assume articulation adds nothing.","Build an end-to-end monolingual speech-translation system that represents speech in articulator space and tests whether the intermediate structure helps.","ArticulateX is an end-to-end monolingual speech translation system operating in articulator space.","The proposed bridge changes the unit of translation: vocal-tract movement is treated as a structured intermediate constraint between sound and language.","The paper reports speech-translation results for the articulator-space system in its tested monolingual setting.","Language, corpus, articulatory estimation, model, references, and evaluation bound generalization; an intermediate representation is not proof of human-like translation."),
"lee25b_interspeech":("An audio-visual system should identify the regions in a video associated with a sound, even for categories or scenes it did not see during training.","Audio and vision have different timing and semantics; zero-shot matching can confuse co-occurrence with the object that actually produced the sound.","Detect objects from vision alone or train a closed-set audiovisual segmenter and reject unseen categories.","Connect pretrained audio and vision models so shared representations can guide zero-shot audiovisual segmentation.","The paper studies zero-shot audiovisual segmentation by bridging pretrained audio and vision models.","Segmentation is grounded association: the system must align a sound event with a spatial region using cross-modal evidence rather than merely classify the clip.","The paper reports zero-shot audiovisual segmentation results for the connected pretrained models.","Datasets, categories, synchronization, pretrained models, and segmentation labels bound the result; co-occurrence does not establish physical source identity."),
"li25i_interspeech":("A TTS system should make emphasis and emotion controllable together, because stressing a word changes how emotion is perceived and emotion changes which emphasis sounds natural.","Text, prosody, and affect are entangled; independent controls can conflict or produce an emphasized contour that does not fit the intended emotion.","Add an emotion label after synthesis or control pitch and energy independently with no relation to the emphasized word.","Model the link between emphasis and emotion explicitly so text position, prosody, and affect can be jointly controlled.","EME-TTS targets the emphasis-emotion link in speech synthesis.","Expressive synthesis is a constrained coordination problem: emphasis is local and linguistic, emotion is broader and affective, and the system must make their interaction coherent.","The paper reports expressive TTS quality and controllability for emphasis and emotion in the tested evaluations.","Languages, speakers, labels, text prompts, control ranges, and subjective raters bound the claim; controllability does not guarantee natural or culturally appropriate expression."),
}
